messages "buggerlugs**To: trillienSubj: Wow, mudmail!Date: Jun  7Hey hon, it's great to hear from you, I never get much mudmail anymore, my only mail since I came back is from Anastasia to tell me she's getting married.  Kevin is actually in the process of moving out...canyou believe it!  But its a very slow process....I don't mind though since we'll soon have theplace to ourselves.  The first time ever!  I can't wait!  We're going to have to buy some furniture,like a coffee table, bookcases and I would like a unit for my ornaments and stuff.  We need a video thoughwhich will take a big chunk, so we're just taking things bit by bit.which will take a big chunk, so we're just taking things bit by bit.Work is pretty good right now, although there's a streak of bad luck going about in our storeour pricingcoordinator suddenly died recently of a heart attack, our supervisor has been hit with a mysterious kidney/back complaint, and our manager has just been admitted for open heart surgery, major bypasses.We just hope that's all our bad luck!Bill and I have started running again, just a mile a day, I hate it, but it should do me some good.  I haveto get my bp down in time for my examination this month, if it's too high she'll take me off the pill.  And I'm not ready for that yet!Anyway, Bill's munching away on dinner so mine must be getting cold in the kitchen, so I'll write morelater and hope you're doing great!  Lucky sods, getting really hot weather, we've had pretty much non-stop rain for the last 2 weeks!*wave*love Sharon**buggerlugs**To: trillienSubj: To the housewife!Date: Jun  8Glad you're gonna start swimming, I love the water.  Well, when it's not pouring out of the sky and isnot preventing me from swimming in the first place!  Mostly the only pools they have over here areopen air ones and they're really small, I'd give anything for an indoor one like the Commonwealth rightnow, I can't stand having to wait til the water is warm enough or the weather is warm.  All this rain isbeginning to remind me of home, the folks at work are frozen stiff, they can't stand these low temperatureswhich are not really low, just the air conditioning is on right now.  I took a few words like glaikit,drookit and scunnered to work yesterday and confused all incredibly.  I love doing stuff like that.  I just have to come up with some more.  You think the americans you have are frustrating, just think about what Ihave to deal with!  HUNGRY americans with food stamps and attitudes!  Drives me nuts!  Matt has this saying\"Must go shopping....have no life\" which is quite apt.  \"Must go shopping....have no life\" which is quite apt.  Anyway, I'm not dressed yet, I have the late shift, 3:30 til midnight, and its still raining, I hope it stopsor I'll have to wake Bill and get him to take me..which I don't like doing too much.or I'll have to wake Bill and get him to take me..which I don't like doing too much.I hate this stupid return button which repeats all I say!!!!!Talk to you soonLove Sharon**buggerlugs**To: trillienSubj: xCc: **Date: Jun  8qqqSorry, couldn't get out of this one.....*blush*qqq**buggerlugs**To: trillienSubj: Hope you had a happy holiday!Date: Jun 24Hi Diane, how was your holiday?  I'm dying for mine, I just have to figure out when I want it, and I'm not sure when that should be.  A whole week without working and still getting paid!  working and still getting paid!  Life here is ok, it's scorching hot right now, so I'm getting some sun, Bill's working todaywhich is a bit of bad luck since I don't get another day off til Saturday and Bill willprobably be working then too.  If the pool wasn't so crowded we'd be in the pool, but there'stoo many kids about, too noisy.  I just set a blanket down on the grass outside and read.Bill's having some political trouble in Wonderland, the wizzes are all starting to fight,and Bill is getting into it too.  I'm enjoying reading everyone attacking each other in sucha petty  way over petty things...isn't that terrible!!!  I need more excitement! I love having an empty apartment!  It stays so clean and tidy when there's just me and Bill.  Except forthe bedroom, where Bill deposits all his clothes and stuff without care!  I won $100 on the lotterya couple of weeks ago, so I bought a clock and a big picture frame and we went to dinner too, it wasgood fun!  We're going to have to buy a video, we may go tonight when he gets home, the NBA draftsare on tomorrow and he wants to see them.Well, I'll probably send more mail later on, I better get some more stuff done.Take care!Love Sharon**buggerlugs**To: trillienSubj: Clean Clean Clean!!!Date: Jul 10Hi hon, well, it's 5pm on the last day off I have for a few hectic days...  Bill's at workand I've spent most of the day cleaning...and it's done!  I can honestly say there's nota whole lot more I could do...Bill has the floors to wash but that's it.. (that's his onlyhousekeeping job).  I tackled the bedroom...the rest was pretty clean anyway, I did it a fewdays ago.  But the bedroom...I can't remember when it was last done..Bill's ALWAYS in here sinceit's where the computer is.  Now the floor is clear, the surfaces are clean, it's tidy and neat..I'm really proud of it.  I've had a couple of days off, Michael came across for a few days, he's working for a pretty goodcompany now, but has been laid off for 3 weeks, he was asking about you.  We went out for dinner theother night, the first time Bill suggested it without it being fast food, and without it beingsuggested to him.  We're in the middle of waiting for out VCR, and Bill's just bought the computergame Twinsen's Odyssey, it's seemingly the newest thing out...it's quite impressive.  I got Baldies, astrategy game which is incredible amounts of fun!  The number of computer game boxes building up isquite bad considering, but Bill is enjoying having the money to buy them.  I'm enjoying not having tocount how much I can spend on anything.  I've been spending a lot of time in the local Hallmark shop,and Bill hasn't complained once, only to tell me he's not following me in there!I'm ready for a change in workplace...our favourite bookstore is hiring...so I'm thinking about it.Well, my chicken is marinating in honey-mustard barbeque sauce, but I've still to figure out what's going with it, it's amazing I'm cooking, it's just for myself, Bill won't be back til late tonight,I never cook for myself...can't be bothered. But tonight I'm going for the works!Well, I'll write again soon, give my love to all!Love and hugsSharon**buggerlugs**To: trillienSubj: hfjsdafhDate: Jul 16Right now it's midnight, and I'm just about to go to bed after a grueling week of work...so I'llsend you all the stuff you need tomorrow when my brain is less cloudy....man what a time we've had at work, shortstaffed and cash short....stressful!See ya soon!Sharon**buggerlugs**To: trillienSubj: hello der!Date: Jul 16Hey, how's it going?  Great to hear from you.  I've been very stressed recently so it's nice to get mail!6am and 12am.  Well, one of them (Bert) got married on Sunday, and 4 of the office went up to New York forhis wedding...leaving 5 of us to cover 3 and a half days work, hectic work considering it was a weekend.Well, only one of us knows how to open the day, and only one other knows how to close.  So Philip had to openevery day, and he had to come back Saturday night to close the week too.  We were very short on cashiers toowhich meant it was really busy...and in the end, our cash was short.  It still is.  Which is very stressful.They all came back yesterday, and Jackie, the customer service manager surprised me by not being upset at being shortso that was good.  But I got yelled at by some ignorant customer who's Western Union money transfer took too long cos of a slow connection.  I broke down!  Can you believe it! Me? Normally I would've taken it allin my stride and been mean back...but i just burst into tears...stupid cow I am.  So Julie, one of the other girlsstarted laying into this woman verbally.  It was good to see.  Anyway, today is my day off and I'm not going todo a bloody thing.  I intend to rest up completely...Bill's working...and although I'll probably handwasha few things and tidy some, I'm going to be lazy, I'm totally worn out.That's most of the reason I'm looking for a new job.  The stress of cash coming up short.  I know that I'm doingeverything right, I'm counting things 3 or four times to make sure...but that doesn't mean everyone else thinksthe same.  I was the last one to enter the office, so naturally I'll be the first one out..and I don't wantthat to hurt my reference or anything..even though I've done nothing wrong.  And I\"m looking for a full time posirion with benefits, right now we have no medical insurance which is scary.  And I'd like to get out ofthe grocery business....it's too scary!  I'd rather one department.  I'm not unhappy...just ready for a change.Up until last week, I've been completely satisfied with everything...I'm just restless now.Apart from work...Bill picked up our VCR yesterday, so that's really good.  Now I can spend all my timewatching bad movies! *laugh*Shaun's party...well I called at the start of it...wrong time totally, noone wanted to speak to me, everythingwas too hectic...in hindsight I shouldn't have called at all.   But I'm ok about it.It's in the 90's now....toooooo hot!  I still walk to work in my shorts...which has a good effect on my tan.And since all the makeup I would wear would slide off my face in the heat...I'm going au naturelle....kind of scary huh!  Now....my email....lets see if I remember correctly...wwelch@uky.campus.mci.netand Rufus' is.....and Rufus' is.....RGHKendall@aol.comthat one's easy.I've been feeling kind of dizzy recently at times, I'm putting it down to the heat...and tiredness.  HopefullyI'll be restored to my natural vigour over the next few days!  We're hoping to take a week off work and go upto his grandmother's estate up in New York next month, if I can get the time off.Well, before this mail becomes longer than time...I'll write again soon, and take care!  And tell David tokeep up on those baby mags...get him used to it so he won't faint in the delivery room! *grin*Love to everyone and happy knicker hunting!Sharon**buggerlugs**To: trillienSubj: oopsDate: Jul 16I think some of the mail got messed up .  At the start I was talking about how there's 10 of us in the officeat work, to cover 6am til 12am.**stanley**To: trillienSubj: It's cold hereDate: Oct 16Dropped in to say hi to you! I'm not on HM nearly asmuch as I used to be (you may have noticed) because I am spending so much time on Wonderland. I got an areaand a quest in, and am recoding fighters, and gee, I guess Im doing a lot there. I am back in school tryingto become an engineer, which means I am no longer livingin Lexington with my brother Silk and his SILLY wifeSharon...as a matter fo fact, I'm 4 hours drive away now.I see that you logged on 4 days ago, so there isstill some hope that you will read this in the sometimenear future. It's time for bed now...goodnight!Stanley (Michael)**stanley**To: trillienSubj: Ask and thou shalt receiveDate: Oct 19I agree it's not the same at all. I log on from time totime to see if anyone I know from the \"old days\" is on, and maybe sit around and pine for the glory days.Anyway, if you ever have the mind, and I am online,I will usually be found at 194.19.24.20 3287. Not a lotof people usually on, but it's better then here, imho.Stanley**"
